+# Derivation and dependency guide
+
+The following gives the final construction's assembly and identifies the written lemmas that must be reviewed. All linked RaD files are pinned at source commit `45d9b60355872041f9275f77c057514def0d45bc`; their SHA-256 values are recorded in `../provenance.json`. They are independently completed campaign arguments, not formal proof objects. The original upstream manuscript and machine/analytic assumptions are retained.
+
+## Actual graph and dirty-register contract
+
+The selected binary triple graph has `h=53`, `v=23426`, `m=h^3=148877`. Its exact allocation has additions `c=571942`, designated outputs `q=70278`, compatible retained links `l=113039`, and physical side roles
+
+$$
+R=c+q-l=529181.
+$$
+
+Three selected clone batches (22898, 14837 and 47) start directly from the original graph, not the older allocation parent's clone jobs. Each clone moves one complete controller chain to a new gate with its first consumer's actual frame. Two new retentions use distinct unused gate capacities; all old links are preserved under explicit endpoint mappings and assigned enlarged frames remain literal. The clone computes the same formal sum, and all later consumers contain its frame. Induction preserves coefficients, forward nesting, reverse complement nesting, terminating pivots, and arbitrary dirty-scratch restoration. Moving a proper subset of a chain and omitting a required retention are rejected small negative controls.
+
+The full separately executed review checked 86,090,550 coefficients, 595,368 logical frames, 3,346,130 physical transitions and 21,697,366 side events. The changed h12 invocation checked 4028 dirty basis vectors in each orientation. These are historical measured checks: the portable arithmetic replay verifies their pinned certificates, not those computations again. The candidate and compiled identities are respectively `439f31afa89e659a2bacb35a7d1474ba67e0410369a5d9cca22dcee4359ff741` and `c7eed569818909583b4df314dd0e05d809c2254905cebf6f6d405a3296f80484`.
+
+Two separately reviewed disjoint payload centers reduce the central loss while preserving the outer boundaries. Payload arithmetic is binary; address frames and metric geometry are rational, later reduced at one eligible odd prime. The two fields must not be conflated.
+
+## Apply eumemic's auxiliary source-frame lemma
+
+Let `D0=B tensor F tensor Q`, of dimension `h^2-h`, and `D1=A tensor F tensor Q`, of dimension `h^2`, with `D0` contained in `D1`. For every stage-two auxiliary use source frame `M=P_D0` and sink frame `I+M`. The scalar invocation restores its arbitrary logical value, so the physical endpoint composition is `Phi_(I+M) Phi_(-M)=Phi_I`. Omitting the added sink `M` fails the retained dirty-input control.
+
+The first actual incidence, including central roles, is the full inverse late gather at `D0`; the last is the full scatter at `D1`. Thus the entrance rank is zero and the exit is
+
+$$
+I+P_{D0}-P_{D1}=I-P_Z,\qquad \dim Z=h.
+$$
+
+The old boundary ranks `2756+146068` equal the new `0+148824`. The relocated family occurs `J=(R+h)v^2=290431698733384` times. No rank mass, role, scalar gate or old source entrance is counted twice. The actual endpoint audit covers all 529181 side roles and 53 centers. Source interpretation adds no scalar/group operation. Credit for this mechanism belongs to eumemic PR13; this package applies it to its own binary triple graph.
+
+## Common metric-isometry and long recursive runs
+
+For a nondegenerate rational metric `G` and nondegenerate kernel `Z` of dimension `d` with `2*d<m`, write `I-P_Z=I-UV`, `VU=I_d`. If the first `d` primal coordinate rows and last `d` dual coordinate columns are invertible, canonical lower/lower elimination has `d` individual off-diagonal pivots and one contiguous diagonal run of length `m-2d`. The individual pivots remain paid children.
+
+One rational `G`-isometry satisfies both flags for the whole finite kernel family. Rational reflections can increase a deficient flag rank by one while preserving previously full flags: every excluded condition is a proper polynomial, and a nonzero finite product has a deterministically searchable integer-grid witness. Iteration constructs the isometry. Source, gate and sink frames are conjugated together, so no runtime basis adapter is free or omitted. This construction makes a simultaneous generic ambient basis, not the nested controlled corner restriction of PR16.
+
+The three credited bit families have kernel dimensions `h`, `2h`, `h^2+h-1`, and corresponding long runs `148771`, `148665`, `143155`, with multiplicities `J`, `J`, `2*v^3`. The families are disjoint actual edges. All other residuals and off-diagonal corners remain individual children. Finite-family table existence and one odd prime excluding all required denominators are constructive setup; the giant objects have not been materialized.
+
+For the protected two-center graph:
+
+| Quantity | Exact value |
+|---|---:|
+| `N` | 12855661152776 |
+| `W` | 606574719772320 |
+| `L` | 4621255125396 |
+| `D=N-2L` | 3613150901984 |
+| `s=W*m-D` | 90305020942392782656 |
+
+The normalized recursive moment, using the exact histogram and outward rational logarithm enclosures, proves the strict bit saving
+
+$$
+a=\frac{583448208746222253}{5\cdot10^{23}}.
+$$
+
+## Complex rows, precision and resampling
+
+The separately accepted h28 shared complex graph has `R_c=88377`, `m_c=21952`. Its three selected boundary classes have whole-residual widths `21168`, `21896`, `21141`. The signed whole-residual identity permits these actual proper children, while native binary adapters and mixed-width product rows are separately paid. No later all-residual PR15/16 complex construction is imported.
+
+The unchanged complex histogram is recertified at phase saving `b=7/(5*10^6)`. The retained semantic child guard has `C1=1`, `C0=32*m*(s+E)^2`, and enhanced complex charge `2*G*W^2+8*s+4*W+4+32*m<E`. With `beta=1/8`, the stopped-leaf saving `(1-beta)*b=1.225e-6` exceeds `a`; the internal exponent stays at the paid bit saving. The old `beta=1/2` fails this additional leaf inequality and is preserved as a negative control.
+
+The new maximum bit width gives exact least halving depth 974 and `W<2^50`; the unchanged complex depth/stock is 272/41. The joint coefficient is `(50*974+41*272)*(2+1/25)=122098.08<123000`. The complete nested reservoir uses `p^123000`, one leading prefix/padding, and suffix `492000*(log2(b_input)+8)`. Earlier reports' `p^73000` stock is superseded for this source-framed construction, rather than silently reused.
+
+Bulk Gaussian resampling is charged through the reviewed phase-cell inverse, locality of principal-window inverses, bounded-halo streams and small mixed-radix local fields. The constant number of global routing changes, source/target lengths, physical cyclic cut, inverse error, line arithmetic, row splitting/padding and restoration are paid. The balanced FFT layout is separately charged through equal-width chunk interchanges and its one extra top bit. A local movement speedup alone is not assumed to imply the final saving.
+
+## Exact final assembly and limits
+
+The portable arithmetic replay reconstructs the native characteristics and complex phase certificate, then checks all twelve combinations of zero/one/two centers, original/balanced layout, and conservative/tight assembly against complete independently produced rows. Each row has all 42 or 43 declared strict conditions, seven extra interface conditions, six joint-stock power checks and six stopped-leaf power checks. This includes the paid tape/resampling and precision interactions, not only scalar additions.
+
+The strongest row uses two centers, the balanced layout and the tight assembly:
+
+$$
+\kappa=\frac{5834475279233921242758637328164947}{5\cdot10^{39}}.
+$$
+
+It is strictly above `2^-20`. Explicit balanced-row numeric conditions share cutoff `log2(b_input)>=258254417031933722624`. Giant fixed table/basis/prime construction, native constants, record domination, strict absorption and the complete upstream-machine threshold remain additional eventual obligations. These qualifications are essential: finite checks and arithmetic do not prove an unconditional multiplication theorem or practicality at the displayed cutoff.
+
